invariant: INV-17
file: src/sha3.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha3-device
reason: SHA3_BELOW_LEN, the bytes of stack sha3.c's entries wipe below their
  bodies, is 704. That covers the bodies' frames for x86-64 and arm64
  under gcc and clang, so bin/sha3_equiv_test passes on every machine's
  own compiler. Under gcc 13.3 for mips32r2 the body under sha3_256
  writes 764 bytes below its caller at -O2 and 708 at -Os, and the wipe
  leaves the deepest of them. The lane's sha3-device part builds the
  binary as a device object for mips32r2 and runs it under qemu-mips,
  where it measures that depth against the length. The lane skips
  without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
#define SHA3_BELOW_LEN 1024
--- new
#define SHA3_BELOW_LEN 704
